cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Academic Hunter"
abstract: >-
  An open-source systematic literature review tool that searches seven academic
  databases in parallel, deduplicates across them, and ranks results with
  Weight-Bleeding — a configurable semantic weighting method that biases a
  bi-encoder's embedding space toward domain terms without fine-tuning, GPU
  compute, or labelled data. Exposes its capabilities as a Model Context
  Protocol server so an LLM agent can orchestrate a review end to end, and runs
  entirely on CPU with no API costs.
